{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nrebar documents a relocatable ticket store as a supported feature, then bypasses its own\nresolver in 13 shipped code paths, each assuming the store sits at `repo_root/.tickets-tracker`.\nAny deployment that relocates the store — which the deployed MCP server does — breaks in those\npaths, with errors naming a path the operator never configured.\n\n## The contract being ignored\n\n`src/rebar/config.py:138-156` (`tracker_dir()`): the env override `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` \"wins\nverbatim\"; otherwise the configured `tracker.dir` applies, where \"an absolute value relocates\nthe store (EV-3b)\". Relocation is a FEATURE, not an edge case.\n\n## Observed failure (live Copilot session)\n\n    bridge_status -> \"cannot read local environment id from\n     /var/gerrit/site/mcp-code/.tickets-tracker/.env-id: [Errno 2] No such file or directory\"\n\nThe server sets `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`; the store is there and healthy\n— 2763 tickets are readable through the same server.\n\n## Root cause (CONFIRMED at runtime)\n\n`_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py:89` composes `repo_root / \".tickets-tracker\" / \".env-id\"`;\nthe caller `_lib_ops.py:288` passes the repo root, never the resolved tracker. The constant at\n`:35` has the same defect for the detail file. Reproduced against a CONTROL arm: same env, same\nstore, `rebar list` succeeds (rc=0) while `rebar bridge status` fails.\n\nAttributed to `b69c-5787-81b8-4052` via commit `fe5a447061cde`. `config.tracker_dir()` already\ncarried the relocation contract at that commit's PARENT, so this is a `plan_defect`, not a\nregression or unmet obligation.\n\n**Triage of all 77 `.tickets-tracker` occurrences (13 defects / 64 legitimate), the\ncaller-dependency sweep, and the RED evidence are in the ticket COMMENTS.**\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\nEach confirmed sibling is its own criterion, ordered by MCP reachability.\n\n**Tier 1 — MCP-reachable and mutating**\n\n- [ ] AC1: `binding_store.py:601` (`load_binding_store`) resolves the binding read/write root.\n- [ ] AC2: `reconcile.py:318` resolves the `prev_snapshot.json` root (and `ctx.tracker_dir`,\n      consumed by `run_differs.py:434`).\n- [ ] AC3: `reconcile.py:456` `check_store_compat` validates the CONFIGURED store, so the\n      fail-closed precheck cannot be defeated by relocation.\n- [ ] AC4: `dispatch_one.py:321` writes `BRIDGE_ALERT` events into the configured store rather\n      than materializing a shadow store at the repo root.\n- [ ] AC5: `git_adapter.py:75` + consumer `reconcile_helpers.py:234` stage the commit-back from\n      the configured store. `TRACKER_DIR` is PRESERVED (exported in `__all__`, pinned by\n      `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_git_adapter_characterization.py:35`); only the consumer\n      changes.\n- [ ] AC6: `_bridge_runner.py:180` passes the RESOLVED tracker to the delivery subprocess.\n- [ ] AC7: `projects_store.py:47` reads and writes the sync mapping in the configured store.\n\n**Tier 2 — MCP-reachable, read/diagnostic**\n\n- [ ] AC8: `last_pass.py:35` resolves the last-pass detail file.\n- [ ] AC9: `last_pass.py:89` reads `.env-id` from the configured store.\n- [ ] AC10: `inbound_translate.py:165` honours the `tracker.dir` key, not only the env override.\n- [ ] AC11: `__main__.py:239` (reconcile-check) loads local tickets from the configured store.\n\n**Tier 3 — CLI-only**\n\n- [ ] AC12: `bridge_fsck.py:663` CLI fallback honours the `tracker.dir` key.\n- [ ] AC13: `__main__.py:508` dry-run enumeration errors rather than silently reporting an\n      empty store when relocated.\n\n**Cross-cutting**\n\n- [ ] AC14: This criterion CREATES `scripts/check_tickets_boundary.py` and wires it into the\n      `lint` target of the `Makefile`. It rejects new store-path composition in `src/`,\n      enforcing the existing `# tickets-boundary-ok` convention with a MANDATORY reason. The 64\n      legitimate occurrences pass. DD1 invokes this script directly; DD2 invokes it via\n      `make lint` — one artifact, both criteria.\n- [ ] AC15: A regression test exercises `bridge_status` with `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` OUTSIDE the\n      repo root, and fails if the hardcoded composition is reintroduced (mutation-checked).\n- [ ] AC16: `bridge_status` is unchanged in the DEFAULT in-tree layout — no regression for the\n      common case.\n- [ ] AC17 LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE. `bridge_status` called through the deployed\n      endpoint returns its status snapshot instead of the `.env-id` ENOENT. Evidence must be\n      OBSERVED against `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` and recorded in a ticket\n      comment naming the tool called, the arguments, and the actual response. A passing local\n      test is NOT sufficient, and neither is a merged change — the container must have\n      redeployed and served the call.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] DD1: AC1-AC13 hold, each routed through `config.tracker_dir()` or the reconciler's\n      already-resolved `ReconcilerSettings.tracker_dir`.\n      Verify: `python scripts/check_tickets_boundary.py`\n- [ ] DD2: AC14's gate is reachable from `make lint` and RED if any drained site regresses.\n      Verify: `make lint`\n- [ ] DD3: AC15's test is RED before the fix and GREEN after; re-introducing the hardcoded path\n      returns it to RED.\n      Verify: `pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_relocated_store.py`\n- [ ] DD4: No regression in the reconciler, bridge, snapshot, or store suites.\n      Verify: `pytest tests/interfaces/facades tests/unit/rebar_reconciler`\n- [ ] DD5: `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean.\n- [ ] DD6: Pre-fix data at the wrong location is dispositioned, NOT migrated. A relocated\n      deployment that ran the mutating paths may hold a stale `<repo_root>/.tickets-tracker/`.\n      No migration is performed: after the fix nothing reads it, so the residue is inert rather\n      than divergent, and auto-deleting a directory rebar no longer interprets is more dangerous\n      than leaving it.\n      Verify: CHANGELOG tells operators to check for and remove that directory manually.\n- [ ] DD7: AC17 observed against the deployed endpoint and recorded in a comment.\n\n## Scope note\n\nSupersedes `cca6-3f7e-dd67-439f` (`addictive-snooty-wildcat`), whose AC1-AC5 cover only\nAC8/AC9 here. Linked `duplicates`."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787861372172265909,"uuid":"a5e8e112-79d9-44fd-b5a8-644381379fb6"}